{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9ezseohh0","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"GOTCHA: setDiagnostics/getDiagnostics — must route through graph-store JSONL, null clears included","summary":"Implementing setDiagnostics(workspaceId, value) / getDiagnostics(workspaceId) by storing in LOCAL_FIELDS or the overlay JSON loses data on config regeneration (overlay JSON is ephemeral). CORRECT PATTERN: (1) Emit a durable event in setDiagnostics: graphStore.appendEvent(store, workspaceId, {evt:\"diagnostics_set\", value, ts}). This MUST happen for ALL values including null — null means \"cleared\". (2) In graph-store.js switch, add: case \"diagnostics_set\": node.diagnostics = ev.value; break — this stores null correctly. (3) In overlay.js load(), rehydrate: base.diagnostics[id] = node.diagnostics (not from JSON). getDiagnostics returns base.diagnostics[wsId] ?? null. The event log replays in order, so the last event wins; if value is null the replay correctly sets node.diagnostics = null. Do NOT skip emitting the event when value is null — skipping means the old value survives a wipe. Discovered during bench: trial 3 passed the non-null durability cases but failed \"null diagnostics survives wipe\" because the implementation did not emit a graph-store event for setDiagnostics(wsId, null).","created_by":"bench-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T11:28:50.832Z","vec":[-0.0544612742960453,0.08130522817373276,-0.007715032435953617,0.10544668138027191,0.02870422601699829,-0.05389246344566345,0.0003594157751649618,0.046329889446496964,-0.023654401302337646,-0.004408353473991156,0.04055685177445412,-0.007094964385032654,0.00518901739269495,0.010050954297184944,-0.011625467799603939,0.04801619425415993,0.01073696929961443,-0.062241870909929276,-0.044753070920705795,-0.04373471066355705,0.024579055607318878,-0.00038253681850619614,-0.008926947601139545,0.0027297085616737604,0.003883164841681719,0.03107028640806675,-0.07592970132827759,-0.02210162952542305,0.0184692721813917